 ### Sync-K-Planes Training
-Sync-K-Planes is a variant of K-Planes adapted for unsynchronized video by incorporating camera-specific time offsets and adjusted time normalization [S1]. It is chosen when dealing with imperfectly synchronized video data, such as the Plenoptic Video Dataset, where fast dynamic contents like flames show different visual appearances in the same frame [S1]. The training involves two versions: hybrid and explicit [S1]. The hybrid version is trained for 90K iterations, and the explicit version for 120K iterations [S1]. An ISG sampling strategy is applied for the first 50K iterations with time offset, followed by an IST sampling strategy for both versions [S1]. The time offset learning rate is set to $0.1\times$ the K-Planes backbone learning rate [S1]. The time normalization range is set to $[-0.8, 0.8]$ to prevent camera-specific time $t_k = t + \delta_k$ from deviating from the feature planes [S1]. On the flame salmon scene, the hybrid version renders in 15.2 min, trains in 2.0 hrs, and has 27.0 M parameters. The explicit version renders in 22.0 min, trains in 3.8 hrs, and has 50.7 M parameters [S1].
